@page "/docs/theming/color-scheme"

@* Light and dark: the app's default, the reader's choice (ColorSchemeSwitch and the ib-scheme
   cookie), a scheme for part of a page, and your own colors in both. From docs/styling.md
   ("Tokens", "A color scheme for part of a page") and components.md (ColorSchemeSwitch). *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="color-scheme">
    <Lead>
        Every color comes in a light and a dark version. Pages follow the device's setting until your app or the user
        picks a scheme, and any part of a page can have its own.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">The app's default</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            To set the app's default scheme, set <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on the <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the
            <Code>head</Code>. <Code>Auto</Code>, the default, follows the device. <Code>Light</Code> or <Code>Dark</Code>
            sets that scheme until the user picks another.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Default</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            In plain HTML, <Code>data-ib-color-scheme="light"</Code> or <Code>"dark"</Code> on the <Code>html</Code> element
            sets a scheme too. It also overrides the user's choice, so use <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> when users can pick.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Let users choose</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A <Anchor Href="docs/components/color-scheme-switch">ColorSchemeSwitch</Anchor> lets the user pick a scheme. It
            comes as a menu of System, Light and Dark for headers, a light/dark toggle, or all three side by side for a
            settings page.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="color-scheme-switch-variants" />
        <TextBlock>
            The choice is kept in the <Code>ib-scheme</Code> cookie. The <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code> reads
            it on the server, so each page arrives in the user's scheme with no flash. Keep an <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> there,
            even an empty <Code>&lt;IzzyTheme /&gt;</Code>. Reading the cookie requires <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code>:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="csharp">@Services</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            With JavaScript off, the switch is hidden, and pages follow the device or a choice saved earlier.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            On interactive pages, <Code>@@bind-Value</Code> gives you the choice as a <Code>ColorScheme</Code>:
            <Code>Auto</Code> for System, <Code>Light</Code> or <Code>Dark</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">A scheme for part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Part of a page can have its own scheme, such as a dark sidebar or header in a light app. Set
            <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on <Code>Box</Code>, <Code>Stack</Code>, <Code>Card</Code> and the other layout
            components, or on a part of the <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-shell">app layout</Anchor>.
            <Code>Dark</Code> and <Code>Light</Code> set that scheme. <Code>Inverse</Code> sets the opposite of the page's,
            even when the page follows the device.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="box-scheme" />
        <TextBlock>
            Every color switches inside that part, so text, links, buttons, badges, fields, focus rings and menus opened
            from it keep their contrast. <Code>Bg</Code> still applies on top: <Code>Bg="Color.Fill"</Code> is that
            scheme's container shade. On your own elements, <Code>data-ib-color-scheme="dark"</Code>, <Code>"light"</Code> or
            <Code>"inverse"</Code> does the same.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Your colors in both schemes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Write a color as a <Code>light-dark()</Code> pair, and one value covers both schemes, including parts of a page
            with their own scheme:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@LightDark</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            If a color shouldn't change with the scheme, give it the same value twice, or use a plain color. Keep text at
            4.5:1 contrast against its background in both schemes.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens">Tokens and customizing</Anchor>: every color as a CSS variable.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/color-scheme-switch">ColorSchemeSwitch</Anchor>: the full API.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Default = """
        <IzzyTheme Preset="ThemePreset.Standard" ColorScheme="ColorScheme.Dark" />
        """;

    private const string Services = """
        builder.Services.AddIzzyBlazor();
        """;

    private const string LightDark = """
        .release-band {
          background: light-dark(#fff7ed, #2a1a0c);
          border-color: light-dark(#fed7aa, #7c2d12);
        }
        """;
}
